[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat V weir and velocity area station. Flow altered by industrial/agricultural abstraction and some effluent returns. GENERAL: Flat V weir and velocity area station. Bankfull channel width 9.1m. STATION HYDROMETRY: Weir 1:20 cross slopes; upstream 1:2; downstream 1:5, bankfull channel width 9.1m. Station in steep valley with flows fairly well contained. Flashy response so obtaining high flow gaugings problematic. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7). Ratings reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1982. FLOW REGIME: Flow influenced by industrial/agricultural abstraction, some effluent returns. The last operational coal mines in this area closed in 1985. Minewater recovery is understood to have occurred by the late 1980s. Mine dewatering increased low flows and mines may have provided some attenuation in flood events.
CATCHMENT,Coal Measures, some Boulder Clay and alluvium in valley. Mainly peaty soils, seasonally wet. Upland area with livestock farming, significant forest cover and urban development in valleys.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to the available gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged above QMED and all recorded flows within bank.
[END]
